# Application model

An Upwell 0.20 application is declared through `app!` around an `App::builder(...)` expression. The builder collects the name and application registrations; the macro declares the host that runs the assembled application.

<Example title="Assemble a small application">

```rust plain
use upwell::prelude::*;

#[component]
struct Inventory;
```

Build the host from that component:

```rust plain
app! {
    App::builder("inventory")
        .with_component(Inventory)
}
```

</Example>

## Keep the boundary explicit

Use the builder chain for values the process owns, including components and protocol integrations. The macro is the application boundary, not a replacement for normal Rust composition inside a component.

This is specifically the 0.20 application declaration. The [1.0 application model](/docs/1.0.0/framework) uses a named `app!` declaration and documents current lifecycle and protocol guidance.
